-- /summary : Analyzer default-export fix, match-path performance, core-types doc refresh
-- /result/0/summary : PR #73 (trail #284) is open and ready, branch fix/default-export-function-kind, based on chore/ratchet-harness-gates. The fix is one new arm in `statement_kind` (analysis/ts/parse.rs) for `ExportDefaultDeclaration`: Function, Class or Interface for those declarations, Other for everything else. Siblings changed: anonymous `export default function () {}` and `export default class {}` (same AST arms), `async` (a function flag), and `export default interface X`. Left as Other: `export default () => {}`, `export default X` and `export { x as default }`, because they are expressions or specifiers and name no declaration kind. Plain `export function` was already Function, so no change. The wrong-behavior pin in `every_top_level_declaration_kind...` and the anonymous test were replaced, and a new rstest covers all 10 cases with exact kinds. The new tests failed before the fix. Added patch changeset default-export-declarations-keep-their-kind.md. Checks run: the harness before and after, and `just ci`. Not run: CI on the PR (pending).
-- /result/0/numbers : Before and after are identical on these: declaration in top 3 58/59, questions 17/18, members 15/16, declaration_in_output 59/59. Axios 'build full path base url' file rank 2 -> 1. Axios 'dispatch request adapter' file rank 2 -> 1. Median output KB per repo is unchanged: zustand 14, zod 41, axios 18.
-- /result/0/decision_log_text : - Decision: `export default` of a function, class or interface declaration takes Function, Class or Interface as its block kind, anonymous and async included.
- Why: the statement_kind arm for ExportDefaultDeclaration returned Other (weight 0.7), so blocks such as axios buildFullPath and dispatchRequest ranked below Function (1.5).
- Rejected: classifying `export default () => {}`, `export default X` and `export { x as default }` as Function or Variable. They carry no declaration kind, and `export const f = () => {}` is already Variable.
- Open: whether a default-exported arrow or function expression should rank as Function; the harness shows no need yet.
-- /result/1/summary : Two changes, PR #74 (trail 285), ready. Both parallelize with rayon and fold in walk order: (1) text_search per-file search (sequential walk, parallel search), (2) pipeline per-file read, parse, block retrieval. Profile on zod (machine loaded, load avg 11-23): text search ~18 ms, retrieve ~18 ms, rank ~4 ms; on 'string optional' dedup is ~30 ms of 51 ms (src/dedup.rs, outside my allowed files, so not changed; report to the dedup owner). Medians over 25 runs, old to new (rg): zod ZodType 34.9 to 20.6 (14.5); parse 46.0 to 20.2 (15.5); safeParse 23.7 to 13.3 (15.0); axios AxiosError 16.5 to 11.3 (12.2); zustand createStore 6.6 to 5.9 (9.1). Byte-identical stdout, stderr and exit code on 99 old/new runs (33 queries x 3 flag sets, 3 repos). Third change not made (remaining cost is dedup). Ran: just ci, rg-compare.py, old/new comparison. Not run: nothing else. Added rayon to the monokl crate (it was workspace-only) and a patch changeset. Caveat: text search now holds all per-file hits before applying the file ceiling.
-- /result/1/numbers : zod ZodType 34.9->20.6 ms (rg 14.5); zod parse 46.0->20.2 (rg 15.5); zod safeParse 23.7->13.3 (rg 15.0); zod 'string optional' 86.5->51.3 (rg 17.1; ~30 ms is dedup); axios AxiosError 16.5->11.3 (rg 12.2); axios request 16.9->11.6 (rg 13.7); zustand createStore 6.6->5.9 (rg 9.1)
-- /result/1/decision_log_text : - Decision: text search and block retrieval fan out per file with rayon and fold results in walk order; the directory walk stays sequential.
- Why: on zod the two stages cost about 18 ms each, sequentially. Folding in order keeps the file ceiling, diagnostics and output byte-identical (99 old/new runs, no diffs).
- Rejected: ignore's build_parallel (walk order would depend on thread timing, which breaks the ceiling and diagnostic order); changing per-file parse thread spawn (inside analysis/**, not measured as the cost).
- Open: dedup_blocks takes about 30 ms of 51 ms on broad queries (1678 candidates, zod 'string optional') and now dominates. Text search holds every file's hits before applying the ceiling, so memory grows on pathological queries past 100k matching files.
-- /result/2/summary : Corrected docs/architecture/core-types.md, the only file changed. The CodeBlock snippet lacked `parent: Option<ParentContext>`, so I added it. I also added a prose note covering four claims:
- `CodeBlock.parent` is the enclosing class or object literal of a member block, and `None` for a top-level block.
- The analyzer sets it (rg: `analysis/ts/mod.rs` tests read `b.parent`).
- Ranking copies it into `RankedBlock.parent_context` (`rank/mod.rs:81`).
- Agent output prints it as the `parent` column, formatted `<kind> <name>` (`output/agent.rs:194,224`).

`symbol_signature`, `matched_lines`, `matched_keywords`, `RankedBlock` and `ParentContext` already matched `types.rs`. Nothing was deleted. No changeset (docs only). PR #72 is ready for review.

Checks: no `just ci` run (docs only), so CI is pending on the PR. Not run: `rg-compare.py`.
